o language change gains user-felt speed. User-felt costs owned by this module: the 1 s sync-convert poll (`converterservice.js:49,163`) and crash-prone untested co-edit code (PKT-0017 fix/crash concentration).\n- Decision: replaced the old DIAG-docservice.md without reading it (independence); DIAG-docservice-b.md did not exist, nothing to `git rm`.\n- Decision: save's 5 s `savetimeoutdelay` is configuration in Common, noted but not planned here.\n- Surprise: `DocsCoServer.js:155` editorStat fallback constructs `editorDataStorage` — folded into P4.\n- Not done: no new measurement (not required; baseline covers the module except the server share of open, listed as a verdict-changer).\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"## Executor log\\n\",log,1)\ns=s.replace(\"## Lessons for the Atlas\\n\",\"## Lessons for the Atlas\\n- docservice: server share of user time is small (co-edit 4 ms p50 server segment); its measured user cost is the sync ConvertService 1 s poll and crash-prone untested DocsCoServer/canvasservice.\\n\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\necho '{\"packet\":\"PKT-0025\",\"role\":\"diagnostician\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"date\":\"2026-11-02\",\"hindered\":{\"ref\":\"diagnosis-verdict#5\",\"text\":\"the spec example header omits goals_hash placement guidance in the plan block; had to infer it goes in the front matter\"},\"missing\":{\"ref\":\"oracle/baseline.md\",\"text\":\"no server-side split of open time (DocService open request to Editor.bin ready), the one number that could change the verdict\"},\"unneeded\":{\"ref\":\"work-packet#target\",\"text\":\"DIAG-docservice-b.md listed in target although it does not exist\"},\"helped\":{\"ref\":\"oracle/baseline.md\",\"text\":\"PKT-0018 co-edit split and PKT-0017 fix concentration answered speed and quality per module directly\"}}' >> .theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl\ngrep -q \"^verdict: \" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-docservice.md && grep -q \"^goals_hash: dcb03039\" .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-docservice.md && echo OK; theseus validate 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Write log, friction, run acceptance"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the docservice diagnosis and committed it. The verdict is **refactor**, staying in JavaScript with no language change. All three acceptance commands pass; `theseus validate` gives 0 errors and one warning, which is the expected one about pilot mode.\n\n**Why refactor:**\n- **Speed:** a change of language would not be felt by users. On the server, receiving and re-sending a co-edit takes 4 ms of a round trip of about 100 ms. Opening a document takes 3–4 s, almost all in the browser. Conversions are 70–90 % the C++ converter (`x2t`).\n- **What this module does cost users:**\n  - A fixed 1 s wait in `converterservice.js:49,163` adds up to 900 ms to every synchronous ConvertService call.\n  - It carries most of the upstream crash fixes, concentrated in `DocsCoServer.js` (4,736 lines) and `canvasservice.js`. Neither file has tests.\n- **What would change the verdict:** if a split of open time showed the server at 10 % or more, or a load test past 1,000 sockets showed the server limiting, I'd reconsider moving the co-edit hot path to Go or Rust. That would need a second diagnosis from another model family (rule D3).\n\n**Packet plan:**\n\n| Key | Wave | Type | What |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | 0 | characterize | Tests for ConvertService in sync and async modes |\n| P2 | 0 | characterize | Tests for the crash-prone co-edit paths in `DocsCoServer.js` |\n| P3 | 1 | refactor | Replace the fixed 1 s poll with a short or growing one (after P1) |\n| P4 | 1 | refactor | Add the missing guards, and fix `editorStat` at `DocsCoServer.js:155`, which is built with the wrong constructor (after P2) |\n| P5 | 0 | investigate | Whether to bring in two upstream crash/hang fixes, bugs 81132 and 81576, that are missing from Euro-Office `main` (a decision for people) |\n\n**Decisions:**\n- I replaced the old `DIAG-docservice.md` without reading it, to keep this diagnosis independent.\n- `DIAG-docservice-b.md` doesn't exist, so there was nothing to `git rm`.\n- Save takes about 6 s mainly because of a 5 s delay set in configuration (`savetimeoutdelay`, in Common). I noted it in the diagnosis but planned no packet for it.\n- I spawned no follow-up packets: the plan block in the diagnosis covers the follow-ups.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** the server is a small part of what users wait for. Its real costs are the synchronous conversion wait and the untested, crash-prone co-edit code.\n\nOne command was refused by permissions: a shell command that used a heredoc to edit the packet file. I made the same edits with the file tools instead.\n\nThe packet's Executor log, its Atlas lessons and the friction line are all written.","ttft_ms":2394,"type":"result","duration_ms":90501,"uuid":"4ee3dbb4-ab4b-4567-acb8-cd50b779633f","ttft_stream_ms":1049,"time_to_request_ms":353,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":182,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":42,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":8,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":25,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":3,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":148,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":